returned_finding_id	P1-authority-not-runtime-bound
returned_finding	The exported runDirectPgRegressionV6({target,evidenceRoot,runCommand}) entry accepts a caller-supplied physical target and has no authority artifact input, no SHA verification for DB/QA/drain/resource GO artifacts, no runId-to-authority binding, and no check that the required independent reviews exist. A caller with Docker access can invoke this entry directly despite the candidate authority's false execution fields.
impact	The stated ordering (isolated fault gate success before a later fresh DB/QA/drain/resource GO chain, and no execution before those gates) is not fail-closed at the execution boundary. The static candidate is safe to review, but is not a runnable GO.
required_correction	Before resource creation or runner execution, introduce a sealed execution authority consumed and verified by the outer executor. It must bind the exact runner SHA, fresh unique runId, dedicated PG16 container full ID, database, anonymous volume, DB GO SHA, QA GO SHA, drain GO SHA, and resource GO SHA; reject absent, false, mismatched, stale, G/H, A-F, shared, production, or prior-resource inputs. Preserve one-attempt/no-auto-retry behavior and leave 000197 plus approval runtime unreachable from this fault-only runner.
status_after_review	NO-GO-for-resource-create-or-execute-until-correction-and-fresh-independent-review
